load; no scanner failures.","timestamp":1788650438391391001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Stage A CL 2690 initial Verified run https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/33998643079 failed in require-ticket before scanner work because the run fetched origin/tickets before the newly created Stage A ticket event was visible. Local verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD resolves 283b-7104-87c1-4015, and a fresh fetch shows origin/tickets now contains the ticket, so I posted a Gerrit recheck as an infrastructure/replication timing retry.","timestamp":1788651773936824001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit had duplicate Stage A CLs 2690 and 2691 with the same Change-Id due the earlier HTTP 504 retry. After abandoning duplicate 2691, Gerrit still rejected patchset updates because abandoned duplicates count for Change-Id uniqueness. I am abandoning 2690 as well and recreating the same validated Stage A diff under a fresh Change-Id; no force/bypass is used.","timestamp":1788652498194124001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Stage A active review change recreated after duplicate Change-Id remediation: CL 2701 https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2701 at commit 5c07545f296d. Prior duplicate CLs 2690/2691 were abandoned; CL 2701 is the same validated Stage A advisory auto-run diff with fresh Change-Id I69e74a09c7ac39c6aba721dc40cb028daf4d923d.","timestamp":1788652592040025001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CL 2701 reached Verified+1 on GitHub run https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/33999972271. LLM-Review was still absent after the documented backfill interval, so I posted the documented Gerrit comment trigger 'rerun-llm-review' for the current revision; this is a review request, not a force/bypass.","timestamp":1788654405322054001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Stage A merged through Gerrit as CL 2701. Gates: Verified+1 on https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/33999972271 and LLM-Review+1 at 2026-09-06 00:38:25Z; submitted at 2026-09-06 00:47:30Z. Gerrit rebased/submitted revision ea08483d825ed5a52534def9f4f175d8b50dd53e, now contained in origin/main.","timestamp":1788656010646676001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## AC6 satisfied — post-merge patchset run observed with a passing scanner-integration job\n\nAC6 required, in its own words, that **after Stage A lands**, a *subsequent* real Gerrit patchset run\nshow the Verified workflow containing a `scanner-integration` job that executes and passes. That\nevidence now exists.\n\n```\nStage A merged (ea08483d825e)      2026-09-06 00:47:30Z\nrun 34005589010                    created 2026-09-06 02:05:59Z   <-- AFTER the merge\n  workflow: change 2704 patchset 1 (rev f322057eba43...)\n  jobs: 21\n  scanner-integration (pinned Semgrep + Gitleaks on the patchset)\n      status:     completed\n      conclusion: success\n      job id:     101412298454\n```\n\nhttps://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/34005589010\n\n### Why this run and not the earlier one\n\nThe previously-recorded run `33999972271` is CL 2701's **own pre-merge** run and does not satisfy an\nAC whose text begins \"After Stage A lands\". The nearest candidate after that, run `34001920346`\n(change 2703 patchset 1), was created at 00:40:46Z — **6 minutes 44 seconds before** the merge — and\nits 21 jobs contain no `scanner-integration` at all, which is itself confirmation that the job only\nappears once Stage A is on `main` (the workflow is dispatched from `main`). Run 34005589010 is the\nfirst patchset run created after the merge, and it has the job.\n\nThat sequence is worth keeping on the record: the job's *absence* at 00:40 and *presence* at 02:05,\nacross the 00:47 merge, is stronger evidence than the passing run alone. It shows the mechanism took\neffect at the merge rather than having been there all along.\n\n### Scope note\n\nThis discharges the advisory stage only. Promotion to Verified voting is Stage B, tracked separately\nas `d645-8f51-0ff9-4070`, whose Gerrit change (2682) is currently `Verified -1` and in WIP under\nrepair. The graph already encodes the ordering — d645 shows `blocked by: 283b-7104-87c1-4015` — so\nthat dependency resolves with this ticket's close and does not need to be re-stated.","timestamp":1788661231107348001}],"created_at":1788641323302053001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c943b10d-f09f-4d83-9ce9-92518158fa98","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"d645-8f51-0ff9-4070"},{"link_uuid":"e649f79c-6b36-49ab-8d29-25cffb638ed4","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2cb1-31b3-7425-4069"}],"description":"## Context\n- This prerequisite story enables the two-stage safe promotion for epic 78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86 and voting story d645-8f51-0ff9-4070.\n- `gerrit-verify.yaml` is dispatched from `main`, so DAG-level changes in a patchset do not run on their own introducing change. Enforcing scanner-integration in the same change that adds its job would recreate the incident-90c7 vacuous-vote class.\n- Stage A therefore lands only an auto-running advisory scanner job. Once this invoker is on `main`, Stage B can observe the scanner job executing on Stage B's own patchset before flipping it into the voting aggregate.\n\n## Scope\n- Add a concrete `scanner-integration` job inside `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml`, gated to the full route like build-and-test/optionality, calling `./.github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml` with Gerrit refspec/project/url so it scans the exact patchset automatically. Invert the two existing tests that currently assert the job is absent from `gerrit-verify.yaml`: `tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py::test_scanner_integration_runs_full_route_but_is_advisory` and `tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py::test_scanner_workflow_is_shared_by_mirror_and_gerrit_advisory` must now assert the job exists and carries the full-route `if:` plus Gerrit patchset inputs while remaining absent from `vote.needs` and vote normalization.\n- Keep the job advisory in Stage A: do not add it to `vote.needs`, do not reference it in vote normalization, and do not remove the `scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py` ADR-0114 advisory exception yet. Because `im-open/workflow-conclusion` observes all jobs in the run, Stage A must also change the vote normalize `CONCLUSION` expression so success is derived from the explicit required-route `needs.*.result` checks (`'success'` when the docs-only or full required route is complete, otherwise `'failure'`) instead of passing through `env.WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION`. The scanner job is not in `vote.needs`, so its failure/cancellation/timeout is visible in the run but cannot cast Verified -1 while advisory; required reusable job failures still block because their `needs.<job>.result` is not `success`. Add a Stage-A test that the normalize expression no longer contains `env.WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION` and still excludes `needs.scanner-integration`.\n- Keep the existing manual `gerrit-scanner-verify.yml` workflow as an on-demand operator probe; the new required evidence for Stage A is that a subsequent real patchset run shows the Gerrit Verified workflow contains a `scanner-integration` job that executes and passes.\n- Update only Stage-A tests and docs needed to distinguish advisory auto-run from voting enforcement. Concretely: invert `tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py::test_scanner_integration_runs_full_route_but_is_advisory` and `tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py::test_scanner_workflow_is_shared_by_mirror_and_gerrit_advisory` to assert the job now exists in `gerrit-verify.yaml` while still absent from `vote.needs` and normalize; add `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py::test_scanner_gate_uses_one_reusable_in_both_lanes_and_stays_advisory`; and add `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` coverage that computes `_workflow_closure((\".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml\",))` and asserts `.github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml` is reachable from the Gerrit root alone. Stage B remains responsible for parity-exception reversal, voting aggregation, and ADR-0114 supersession.\n\n## Anti-90c7 safety design\n- No enforcement changes land in Stage A, so a scanner failure cannot block all merges while the auto-run invoker is being introduced.\n- Empirical GHA proof is required after Stage A lands: observe a real Gerrit patchset Verified run from `main` with `scanner-integration` present, executed, and passing. Record the run URL/job id on this ticket and on d645 before starting Stage B submit decisions.\n- Portability remains through the existing portable `make scanner-integration` target and `_scanner-integration.yml` wrapper; Stage A introduces no bash-only Make recipe and no GitHub-only scanner implementation.\n\n## Testing\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py::test_scanner_workflow_is_shared_by_mirror_and_gerrit_advisory -q` proves the scanner job is auto-run from `gerrit-verify.yaml`, remains out of `vote.needs` and vote normalization, the vote normalize expression ignores all-run `env.WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION` while deriving success from explicit required-route results, and `_workflow_closure((\".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml\",))` reaches `_scanner-integration.yml` from the Gerrit root alone (not merely through `test.yml`).\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py` must still pass with `scanner-integration` excluded as advisory.\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint && env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck` proves repo gates remain green.\n- Sandboxed mutation removes the advisory scanner job from `gerrit-verify.yaml` and confirms the held-out tests fail, then restores.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Newly-added assertions in `pytest tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py`, plus inverted assertions in `tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py` and `tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py::test_scanner_workflow_is_shared_by_mirror_and_gerrit_advisory`, prove `gerrit-verify.yaml` contains a full-route advisory `scanner-integration` job using `_scanner-integration.yml` with Gerrit patchset inputs; these are Stage-A coverage updates.\n- [x] `pytest tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py` proves Stage A keeps `scanner-integration` out of `vote.needs` and out of vote normalization, and proves the normalize expression derives `CONCLUSION` from explicit required-route `needs.*.result` checks without `env.WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION`, so the advisory scanner job cannot cast Verified -1 through the all-run conclusion.\n- [x] `python scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py` still passes with `scanner-integration` documented in `EXCLUDED_JOBS` as the temporary Stage-A advisory exception.\n- [x] `pytest tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` includes an assertion over `_workflow_closure((\".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml\",))` proving the auto-running scanner reusable is reachable from the Gerrit-only Verified workflow closure, so future patchsets exercise it from `main` independently of the existing mirror `test.yml` scanner job.\n- [x] `make lint && make typecheck` pass locally with `.venv/bin` first on PATH.\n- [x] [non-codebase] After Stage A lands, a ticket comment records the real GHA run URL/job id showing `scanner-integration` executed and passed on a Gerrit patchset before Stage B enforcement is submitted.\n      provenance: environment=github-actions runner (navapbc/rebar, gerrit-verify.yaml dispatched from main); principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — queried the GitHub Actions API for run 34005589010 (change 2704 patchset 1, created 2026-09-06T02:05:59Z, after Stage A merged as ea08483d825e at 00:47:30Z) and read job `scanner-integration (pinned Semgrep + Gitleaks on the patchset)`, id 101412298454, status=completed conclusion=success. Control: run 34001920346 (created 00:40:46Z, 6m44s BEFORE the merge) enumerates 21 jobs and contains no scanner-integration job, so the job's presence is attributable to Stage A landing rather than pre-existing. This is a read-only observation of the real production CI system; no privileged mutation was required or performed.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml","reason":"Add full-route advisory scanner-integration job on Gerrit patchsets without voting aggregation."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py","reason":"Assert Stage-A scanner job remains advisory and outside vote normalization."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py","reason":"Assert Gerrit Verified auto-runs scanner reusable with patchset inputs."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py","reason":"Assert scanner reusable is reachable from Gerrit Verified closure for future patchsets."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py","reason":"Update scanner workflow sharing test for auto-run advisory shape."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"],["relates_to","2cb1-31b3-7425-4069"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"1988524e-6c1f-4424-87e0-f04741c50943","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"stat